<%# One post of the thread: the words, the count, an optional link, and the card that each network
    will render for that link.

    ⚠️ **Both fields must render for every block, in the same order.** The names are `posts[][text]`
    and `posts[][link]`, and Rails starts a new hash when a key repeats. A block that omits one
    field would move each pair below it by one. There is no index in the name, on purpose: an index
    needs renumbering in the browser at each add and each remove.

    ⚠️ Each block is its own `social-post` controller. That is what keeps the count, the spinner,
    and the preview of one post away from the others.
%>
<%# ⚠️ The Bluesky map is a plain data attribute and NOT a Stimulus value. A value arrives through
    a MutationObserver, thus it is not synchronous, and `social#canPost` reads the count line that
    this block writes. The button would then follow the keystroke before the current one. %>
<div class="social-post" data-social-target="post" data-controller="social-post"
     data-social-post-bluesky-mentions="<%= mentions_json %>"
     data-social-post-preview-url-value="<%= social_preview_path %>"
     data-social-post-limit-value="<%= limit %>"
     data-social-post-warn-at-value="<%= warn_at %>">

  <%# A line between two posts. It is on each block and the first one hides it, thus a block that
      the browser clones needs no extra markup. %>
  <wa-divider class="social-post__divider"></wa-divider>

  <%# ⚠️ Everything but the divider is in this wrapper, and the wrapper owns the gap between the
      fields. Without it that gap would also apply below the divider, and the space above the line
      could never match the space below it. Refer to _social.scss. %>
  <div class="social-post__body">
    <%# ⚠️ The HANDLE carries `draggable`, and never the block. A draggable block takes the pointer
        away from the fields inside it, thus a person could not select the words of their own post.
        ⚠️ It is a real button and it takes the keyboard: the arrow keys move the post. A drag needs
        a pointer, and this page must work without one. It is hidden while there is one post.
        It sits in the gutter column of the grid, beside the label of the field. Refer to
        _social.scss. %>
    <wa-button class="social-post__handle" appearance="plain" size="small" draggable="true"
               data-social-target="handle"
               data-action="dragstart->social#dragStart dragend->social#dragEnd
                            keydown->social#movePostByKey">
      <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "grip-dots-vertical") %>
      <span class="wa-visually-hidden">Reorder this post with the arrow keys</span>
    </wa-button>

    <%# ⚠️ The icon is in the DEFAULT slot and not in `start`. With `start` and no label, the button
        keeps the width of a label that is not there and the icon sits off to one side.
        ⚠️ `<wa-button>` makes a square icon button only for a `<wa-icon>` child, and this app never
        uses that element (it needs a kit code that this configuration has not). Thus _social.scss
        gives the square. It is hidden while there is one post: a thread of one has nothing to
        remove. %>
    <wa-button class="social-post__remove" appearance="plain" size="small"
               data-social-target="remove" data-action="click->social#removePost">
      <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "circle-xmark") %>
      <span class="wa-visually-hidden">Remove this post</span>
    </wa-button>

    <%# ⚠️ No `maxlength` and no `with-count`. Both measure UTF-16 code units, and Bluesky counts
        graphemes: one emoji is 1 there and 2 or more here. The count line below is ours, and it
        warns and never stops a keystroke. %>
    <wa-textarea name="posts[][text]" label="Post" rows="5" resize="auto" required
                 value="<%= post.text %>"
                 placeholder="What do you want to say?"
                 data-social-post-target="body"
                 data-action="input->social-post#count">
    </wa-textarea>

    <%# The server writes the first value, thus the line has its height before the JavaScript runs
        and the page does not move. The controller writes each value after that.
        ⚠️ The number is the length of the text that BLUESKY will get, after the handles go in.
        Bluesky has the shortest limit and "@tony" grows into a domain, thus a count of the words
        alone would let a draft through that Bluesky then refuses. SocialPresenter#bluesky_length
        makes it, and this view holds no count of its own. %>
    <p class="social__count wa-caption-s" aria-live="polite"
       data-social-post-target="count"><%= count %> / <%= limit %></p>

    <%# ⚠️ The link is OPTIONAL and it has no `required`: a post can be words alone. There is no
        list of the articles here, on purpose: the card comes from the og: tags of whatever page
        this names, thus a link to another site needs no more code. %>
    <wa-input type="url" name="posts[][link]" label="Link"
              value="<%= post.link %>"
              placeholder="https://"
              autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
              data-social-post-target="link"
              data-action="input->social-post#schedulePreview change->social-post#schedulePreview">
      <%# It spins for the whole wait: the debounce and then the request. ⚠️ It needs a rule for
          `[hidden]`; refer to _social.scss. %>
      <wa-spinner slot="end" class="social__spinner" data-social-post-target="spinner" hidden></wa-spinner>
    </wa-input>

    <%# The card that each network will render. The controller fills it and shows it, thus it is
        empty and hidden until the owner pastes a link.
        ⚠️ `with-media` is not in this markup: a page can have no picture, thus the controller sets
        it with the image. %>
    <wa-card class="social-card" data-social-post-target="preview" hidden>
      <img slot="media" class="social-card__image" data-social-post-target="previewImage" alt="" hidden>

      <%# ⚠️ This is the useful part: it says which of the two cards Bluesky will render, and the
          owner cannot know that until after the post without it. %>
      <wa-badge class="social-card__kind" appearance="outlined"
                data-social-post-target="previewKind"></wa-badge>
      <p class="social-card__host wa-caption-s" data-social-post-target="previewHost"></p>
      <p class="social-card__title" data-social-post-target="previewTitle"></p>
      <p class="social-card__description" data-social-post-target="previewDescription"></p>
    </wa-card>
  </div>
</div>
